---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How pricing works — CanYouDo?">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">Pricing</p>
      <h1>Their rate, plus our service charge. Nothing hidden.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--ink-600)">There is no fixed price on CanYouDo?. Every cleaner sets their own hourly rate. We add a service charge of <strong>20%</strong> on top of that rate, and you see the combined total before you book.</p>

      <div class="price-split" style="margin:30px 0" role="img" aria-label="The provider's own rate plus a 20% service charge">
        <div class="part worker"><span class="amount">Cleaner's rate</span><span class="who">set by them · paid to them directly, in full</span></div>
        <div class="part platform"><span class="amount">+ 20%</span><span class="who">our service charge · paid online</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The cleaner's rate</h3>
          <p>Each provider publishes their own hourly rate on their profile, based on their experience, their area and the work involved. They're paid that rate directly by you — we never touch it and we never take a commission from it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Our 20% service charge</h3>
          <p>Calculated on the cleaner's rate and added on top, so it's always visible. It funds the notice board: bookings, calendars, automatic emails, messaging, reviews and gradings, and human customer support.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top:52px">Two payments, two purposes</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Who it goes to</th><th>How it's paid</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>The hourly rate for the cleaning</td><td>Your cleaner</td><td>Directly to them (their preferred method, shown once your booking is confirmed)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>The 20% service charge</td><td>CanYouDo?</td><td>Online when you book</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-top:10px">Keeping the two separate is the point: it means the cleaner's earnings are never eroded by our fee, and you can always see exactly what each part is for.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:52px">Urgent and one-off work</h2>
      <p>Need someone at short notice? You can flag a request as urgent, which offers the cleaner an agreed uplift on their own rate for taking on the job at short notice. The uplift goes to <strong>them</strong>, not to us — our service charge simply applies to the agreed total as usual. Cleaners are always free to decline.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:52px">Gradings, not discounts</h2>
      <p>We don't run races to the bottom. Instead, cleaners earn a grading from their reviews — <strong>New</strong>, <strong>Rising Star</strong>, <strong>Trusted</strong>, <strong>Elite</strong> and <strong>Superstar</strong> — based on punctuality, completing the work asked for, and overall ratings. It rewards doing the job well rather than undercutting.</p>

      <div class="notice notice-info" style="margin-top:34px">
        <strong>What you'll see:</strong> every profile and every booking shows the cleaner's rate, the service charge and the combined hourly total, before you commit to anything.
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:30px"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/find-a-cleaner/">Find a cleaner</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
